<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nubians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nubians are a people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> who speak Nubian languages. Their ancestors created the kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerma">Kerma</a> and Kush and the Christian states of Nobadia, Makuria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alodia">Alodia</a>, before gradual <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamisation">Islamisation</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabisation">Arabisation</a> from the 14th century. In the 1960s the reservoir of the Aswan High Dam flooded much of their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>, displacing tens of thousands of people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nubians.jpg" alt="Nubians" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mohammed Moussa · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nubians_at_Aswan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
